  "raw_text": "176\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb&dba-2 Timoti 3:2\n):\n \nupla nani ba klauna ai dukiara baman luki kabia\n \n–\n \npeople will only be thinking about themselves\n \n/ la\ngente solo estará pensando en sí mismos\n;\n \n(\nlrw-2 Timoti 3:2\n):\n \nupla nani lika on ai winara man latwan kaiki kabia bamna\n;\n \n(\ndbta-\n2 Timoti 3:2\n):\n \nupla nani ba on ai wina dukia baman pliki bangwi kabia\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-1Cor4:12\n):\n \non miti nani ni work takisni\n \n–\n \nwork with our own hands\n \n/ trabajar con nuestras propias manos)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-1Cor7:7\n):\n \nupla bani on ai presentka brisa\n \n–\n \neach one has his own gift\n \n/ cada uno tiene su propio don)\n \nTo what extent are\n\nOn\n \nand\n \nKlauna\n \nused in everyday speech?\n \nNote that\n \ndict\n \nand\n \ndictu\n \nalso give the definition for\n \nOn\n \nas\n \noneself\n \nbut haven’t found\n\nthat usage so far.\n\nOseas\n \n(\ndb,dbta\n;\n \nHosiya\n-\nbw\n;\n \nHusiya\n-\ndba\n)\n \n–\n \nHosea\n \n(Bible book) / Oseas (libro bíblico)\n\nPabula\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmosquito net\n \n/ mosquitero\n\nPadin\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npardon, forgiveness\n \n/ perdón\n\nPadin lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nPadin munaia lâka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nforgiveness\n \n/ perdón\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nSwih tikan lâka\n)\n\nPadin munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto forgive\n \n/ perdonar\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nSwih tikaia\n)\n\nKupia wina padin munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto forgive from the heart\n \n/ perdonar desde el corazón\n\nPadin muni ba\n \n–\n \nforgiveness\n \n/ perdón\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nPadin lâka, Swih tikan lâka\n)\n\nPah\n \n(Onomatopoeia\n \n/ Onomatopeya)\n \n–\n \nthis onomatopoeia adds the idea of:\n \nsatisfaction\n \nor\n \nsurprise\n \n/ esta onomatopeya\n\nagrega la idea de: satisfacci\nó\nn o sorpresa\n\nÂuyapah\n \n(Auyapah, Auya pah)\n \n(\ndb,dictu,dict,mwb,fg,sn,bh,bm,sjjyls,fy,km,lfb\n;\n \nÂuya pah\n-\nhf,lff,sjjyls\n)\n \n(\nadj,adv)\n \n–\n \nsatisfied,\n\ncontent, pleased, satisfactorily, contentedly\n \n/ satisfecho, contento\n\n(Construct:\n \nÂiyapah\n;\n \nÂmyapah\n)\n\nÂmyapah pis!\n \n–\n \nEnjoy your meal!\n \n/ Buen provecho!\n\nÂuyapah daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto satisfy\n \n/ satisfacer\n\nÂuyapah lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsatisfaction, contentedness\n \n/ satisfacción\n\n(Construct:\n \nÂiyapah lâka, Âmyapah lâka\n)\n\nÂuyapah takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be satisfied, to be pleased, to be content, to become satisfied, to become pleased,\nto become content\n \n/ estar satisfecho, estar contento\n\nÂuyapahkira\n \n(adj,adv)\n \n–\n \nsatisfied, content, pleased, contentedly\n \n/ satisfecho, contento\n\nKupia pah\n \n–\n \nsatisfied heart, happy heart\n \n/ corazón satisfecho, corazón contento\n\nPah takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto appear\n \n/ aparecer\n\n(Ex/Ej(\n2 Sam 18:9\n):\n \nDebit suliarka (Absalón) mawan kat pah takan\n \n–\n \nDavid’s soldiers appeared in front of Absalom\n \n/ Los\nsoldados de David aparecieron frente a Absalón)\n\nPahbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto sweep\n \n/ barrer\n\nLata pahbaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nyard sweeper, outside sweeper, rake\n \n/ barredora de jardín, barredora exterior, rastrillo\n\nPahni\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ninheritance, something that belonged to someone who is now deceased\n \n/ herencia, algo que pertenecía a\nalguien que ahora ha fallecido\n\nPahpaya\n \n(a/t:\n \nPahpaia\n,\n \nPahpya\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nshoulder\n \n/ hombro\n\n(Construct:\n \nPaihpaya\n \n–\n \nmy shoulder\n \n/ mi hombro;\n \nPamhpaya\n \n–\n \nyour shoulder\n \n/ tu hombro;\n \nAi pahpaya\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their shoulder\n \n/\nsu hombro)\n\nPain\n \n(adj,adv)\n \n–\n \nfine, good, pretty, well\n \n/ bien, bueno, bonita, guapa\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb81\n):\n \nYawan upla sut wal pain bara kasak kaia sa, wan waihla nani wal kat sin.\n \n–\n \nWe must be good and fair to everyone,\neven with our enemies.\n \n/ Debemos ser buenos y justos con todos, incluso con nuestros enemigos.)\n\nKau pain\n \n–\n \nbetter, best\n \n/ mejor, el mejor\n\nPain apia sa\n \n–\n \nis not fine/good\n \n/ no está bien\n\nPain nu kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto know well, to be knowing well, to be certain, to be sure\n \n/ saber bien, estar sabiendo bien,\nestar seguro\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nSetan pain nu sa...\n \n–\n \nSatan is knowing well...\n \n/ Satanás lo sabe bien...\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n02/19\n):\n \nDîa muni yawan pain nu kaia sa\n \nGâd ra mayuni ba, tânka kasak ba wina daukisa sapa?\n \n–\n \nWhy must\n\nwe know for sure whether our worship of God is made from (\nor\n \nbased on) truth?\n \n/ ¿Por qué debemos saber con certeza si\n\nnuestra adoración a Dios está hecha de (o basada en) la verdad?\n)\n\nPain pali\n \n–\n \nvery fine, very good, very well\n \n/ muy bueno, muy bien\n\nPain sa\n \n–\n \nis fine/good\n \n/ está bien\n\nPain wabia\n \n(v-3p-fut-II; irrealis)\n \n–\n \nwill go well, to go well, will have success, to have success\n \n/ irá bien, saldrá bien,\nque salga bien, tendrá éxito, que tenga éxito",
